Overlay patch 0031: stereoscopic eye rendering for visionOS 3D (D-030 M3/M4).
The shell's CompositorServices loop (SohImmersive.m) composites two per-eye
Metal textures onto a world-locked panel. This patch makes Fast3D produce
them: in 3D mode (gSoh3DMode, shell-owned), Fast3dWindow runs the interpreter
TWICE per host frame — same game time, same command list — with an eye state
that (a) swaps mGameFb to a per-eye framebuffer (all existing offscreen
plumbing then targets it transparently), and (b) applies an off-axis stereo
projection to PERSPECTIVE matrices only (vkQuake patches/0010 math, row-vector
transposed): camera shift folded into P as P'[3][j] -= e*P'[0][j], and the
convergence skew P'[2][0] -= P'[0][0]*e/C so zero parallax sits at C — ortho
(HUD/2D) stays untouched and therefore exactly on the panel plane. The screen
framebuffer (fb 0) is NEVER touched in 3D: no drawable acquire (a hidden
window's acquire stalls forever), no present — a new Metal EndFrameOffscreen
commits the drawn framebuffers, runs 0019's pending-mip pass, and does
EndFrame's state cleanup. Both eyes render EVERY host frame (alternating
halves each eye's rate and reads as judder). Engine dims are overridden to
the eye render size during a pass and restored on exit. CVars:
rev2 (device feedback): convergence is ADAPTIVE — anchored on the smoothed
camera-to-focus distance exported by 0032, biased by gSohIos.StereoConvBias
(default 1.0); the eye offset is gSohIos.StereoDepth (default 0.025) TIMES
the convergence, so background disparity is scene-constant. Fixed sep/conv
made depth swing wildly with OoT's camera distance (uphill-intense,
field-flat, near-ground diplopia — all one root cause).
All new code is __IOS__-guarded; the shell globals live in SohIosShell.m so
iPhone links resolve (mode simply stays 0 there); macOS compiles none of it.

